# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit the real .env.
#
# ---- Local development (phones/emulators on the same WiFi/LAN as this host) ----
# Set both to this machine's LAN IP (e.g. `ip addr` / `ifconfig`, something
# like 192.168.1.50). A loopback address (127.0.0.1) will NOT work for
# TURN_RELAY_IP -- a relay socket bound to loopback cannot forward packets to
# a real peer, only to itself.
#
# TURN_LISTENING_IP=192.168.1.50
# TURN_RELAY_IP=192.168.1.50
# TURN_EXTERNAL_IP=192.168.1.50
#
# ---- VPS deployment (real phones on different networks/carriers) ----
# TURN_LISTENING_IP and TURN_RELAY_IP are the VPS's own interface address
# (often 0.0.0.0 works too, but an explicit private/interface IP is safer
# with `network_mode: host`). TURN_EXTERNAL_IP is the VPS's PUBLIC IP -- the
# address phones on the internet will actually be told to send media to. If
# the VPS's interface IP differs from its public IP (common behind a cloud
# provider's NAT), coturn also accepts `--external-ip=<public>/<private>`;
# in that case set TURN_EXTERNAL_IP to that combined value.
#
# TURN_LISTENING_IP=10.0.0.5
# TURN_RELAY_IP=10.0.0.5
# TURN_EXTERNAL_IP=203.0.113.7

TURN_LISTENING_IP=
TURN_RELAY_IP=
TURN_EXTERNAL_IP=

TURN_PORT=3478
TURN_MIN_PORT=49160
TURN_MAX_PORT=49200

# Any client presenting these credentials can relay through this server --
# treat them like a password. Generate a real one, e.g.: openssl rand -hex 16
TURN_USERNAME=changeme
TURN_PASSWORD=changeme

TURN_REALM=voicecall.local

# Optional. Browsers only allow getUserMedia() on a secure context (https://
# or http://localhost) -- a plain http://<LAN-IP>:3002 origin can't prompt
# for mic access at all (see README.md's "Microphone access needs a secure
# context"). If you're fronting the web client with a reverse proxy on a real
# domain, set this to that https:// origin. Your proxy only needs one rule,
# to the web container's port 3002 -- the web app proxies /socket.io to the
# backend (port 3001) itself (see vite.config.ts's routeRules), since once
# the page loads over https the browser would otherwise block a plain http://
# signaling connection as mixed content. TURN URLs are exempt from that
# restriction, so VITE_TURN_URL above doesn't need to change. Leave unset to
# keep using the plain-http LAN address below.
#
# PUBLIC_SIGNALING_URL=https://app.example.com
